## Architectural Significance

The Lender Intake OS V2 demonstrates that borrower intake can be implemented as a bounded, multi-workflow operating system rather than as a single monolithic automation.

Each workflow owns a defined responsibility while coordinating through persistent state, standardized eligibility contracts, processing locks, deterministic transitions, and governance records. Together, the four workflows form an operational conveyor that converts an external borrower submission into an authorized, validated, traceable, and processing-ready application.

